From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:20:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] main: end the helpers with SIGTERM when netifd exits

On exit, netifd_kill_processes() ends every helper with SIGKILL, so a
DHCP client does not release its lease. Since a helper now gets SIGTERM
when netifd crashes, a normal exit ends it differently from a crash.

Send SIGTERM to the helpers on exit, like the crash path. udhcpc then
releases its lease, since dhcp.sh runs it with -R, and so does odhcp6c,
which dhcpv6.sh runs without -k; pppd ends its session. A network
restart or a reboot thus releases the WAN lease and the delegated
prefix. The other callers of netifd_kill_process() keep SIGKILL.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
(cherry picked from commit edfe9877ee7dc60eb0cd5d9bb15a787c9489c012)
---
 main.c | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
index 2c51ab1..8c1bf1d 100644
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -270,17 +270,23 @@ error:
 	return -1;
 }
 
-void
-netifd_kill_process(struct netifd_process *proc)
+static void
+__netifd_kill_process(struct netifd_process *proc, int signo)
 {
 	if (!proc->uloop.pending)
 		return;
 
-	kill(proc->uloop.pid, SIGKILL);
+	kill(proc->uloop.pid, signo);
 	uloop_process_delete(&proc->uloop);
 	netifd_delete_process(proc);
 }
 
+void
+netifd_kill_process(struct netifd_process *proc)
+{
+	__netifd_kill_process(proc, SIGKILL);
+}
+
 static void netifd_do_restart(struct uloop_timeout *timeout)
 {
 	execvp(global_argv[0], global_argv);
@@ -351,8 +357,9 @@ netifd_kill_processes(void)
 {
 	struct netifd_process *proc, *tmp;
 
+	/* SIGTERM lets a DHCP client release its lease */
 	list_for_each_entry_safe(proc, tmp, &process_list, list)
-		netifd_kill_process(proc);
+		__netifd_kill_process(proc, SIGTERM);
 }
 
 int main(int argc, char **argv)
